1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,206
Stop adding workers.

2
00:00:01,206 --> 00:00:02,246
Look at this pile.

3
00:00:02,246 --> 00:00:06,454
Eight workers are holding jobs; only two jobs are getting through.

4
00:00:06,467 --> 00:00:09,578
Those orange blocks are waiting, not doing extra work.

5
00:00:09,578 --> 00:00:12,740
This is simulated traffic, not a live AI crash.

6
00:00:12,767 --> 00:00:14,263
Here comes another pair.

7
00:00:14,263 --> 00:00:18,266
The door opens, the pile drops, and the next two squeeze through.

8
00:00:18,266 --> 00:00:19,616
Nobody disappears.

9
00:00:19,633 --> 00:00:21,383
I'm giving you the controls next.

10
00:00:21,383 --> 00:00:26,367
Before we touch that worker switch, watch what this little doorway can actually clear.

11
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,316
Twelve jobs.

12
00:00:27,316 --> 00:00:28,250
Four workers.

13
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:28,781
Go.

14
00:00:28,781 --> 00:00:33,838
The blue blocks prepare; the white lanes process; the green blocks are finished.

15
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:35,212
Follow the exits.

16
00:00:35,212 --> 00:00:36,662
Another pair, then another.

17
00:00:36,662 --> 00:00:39,722
The next pair is already waiting when a lane opens.

18
00:00:39,722 --> 00:00:41,109
Keep your eye on twelve.

19
00:00:41,133 --> 00:00:43,436
Twelve point five simulated seconds.

20
00:00:43,436 --> 00:00:44,785
That's our time to beat.

21
00:00:44,785 --> 00:00:47,773
The orange pile never held more than two waiting jobs.

22
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:49,696
Same twelve jobs on the replay.

23
00:00:49,696 --> 00:00:53,190
Same half-second preparation and two-second tool service.

24
00:00:53,190 --> 00:00:55,027
I'm leaving those settings locked.

25
00:00:55,027 --> 00:00:57,068
Only the worker switch gets a turn.

26
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:59,222
First, take two workers away.

27
00:00:59,222 --> 00:01:00,514
See that empty doorway?

28
00:01:00,514 --> 00:01:02,973
Both workers are preparing the next pair.

29
00:01:02,973 --> 00:01:04,810
Nothing passes during that gap.

30
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:05,792
There it is again.

31
00:01:05,792 --> 00:01:09,816
Green blocks leave, blue blocks prepare, and the doorway waits.

32
00:01:09,816 --> 00:01:12,395
Watch the last pair crawl toward the finish.

33
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,553
Fifteen seconds.

34
00:01:13,553 --> 00:01:14,029
Slower.

35
00:01:14,029 --> 00:01:16,070
So more workers helped us before.

36
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:20,061
The four-worker run filled those gaps and finished at twelve point five.

37
00:01:20,067 --> 00:01:23,797
Look at the doorway now: busy while the next pair gets ready.

38
00:01:23,797 --> 00:01:25,049
Four workers feed it.

39
00:01:25,049 --> 00:01:26,828
What happens when we give it eight?

40
00:01:26,833 --> 00:01:27,985
Follow job four.

41
00:01:27,985 --> 00:01:29,301
Blue, then orange.

42
00:01:29,301 --> 00:01:33,823
Its worker is still occupied, but the job cannot enter either white lane yet.

43
00:01:33,833 --> 00:01:35,113
Now a lane opens.

44
00:01:35,113 --> 00:01:38,264
Job four moves in; its worker stays attached.

45
00:01:38,264 --> 00:01:40,969
Watch that badge follow the job all the way out.

46
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,256
The other orange blocks wait their turn.

47
00:01:43,256 --> 00:01:47,825
More occupied worker boxes would not magically carve another opening in this wall.

48
00:01:47,825 --> 00:01:49,184
Here comes the replay.

49
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,088
Same jobs.

50
00:01:50,088 --> 00:01:51,226
Same two slots.

51
00:01:51,226 --> 00:01:55,091
Keep that picture in your head, because you're about to bet on the next run.

52
00:01:55,091 --> 00:01:57,294
No changing the jobs after guessing.

53
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,602
I just doubled the workers from 4 to 8.

54
00:01:59,602 --> 00:02:02,670
Does the processing speed double, or does the system choke?

55
00:02:02,670 --> 00:02:03,783
Lock in your guess.

56
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:07,331
Go.

57
00:02:07,331 --> 00:02:08,184
There they go.

58
00:02:08,184 --> 00:02:11,610
Six orange blocks pile up against the same two openings.

59
00:02:11,633 --> 00:02:13,264
The door keeps draining pairs.

60
00:02:13,264 --> 00:02:14,094
No crash.

61
00:02:14,094 --> 00:02:17,373
Watch the final pair: the finish line has not moved.

62
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,576
Twelve point five.

63
00:02:18,576 --> 00:02:19,906
Traffic jam wins.

64
00:02:19,906 --> 00:02:22,467
More waiting at the tool, not double speed.

65
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:23,369
Look left.

66
00:02:23,369 --> 00:02:25,294
The input queue emptied faster.

67
00:02:25,294 --> 00:02:27,185
Looks like an upgrade, right?

68
00:02:27,185 --> 00:02:29,725
Now look at the orange tower beside the tool.

69
00:02:29,733 --> 00:02:31,101
That's where the waiting went.

70
00:02:31,101 --> 00:02:32,708
Six piled up at the peak.

71
00:02:32,708 --> 00:02:36,258
The lanes keep draining it; the service clock hasn't sped up.

72
00:02:36,267 --> 00:02:37,954
Replay with four workers.

73
00:02:37,954 --> 00:02:40,989
Smaller orange pile, more jobs waiting on the left.

74
00:02:40,989 --> 00:02:42,269
We didn't delete the work.

75
00:02:42,269 --> 00:02:43,921
We moved the waiting room again.

76
00:02:43,933 --> 00:02:46,332
Watch both counters as the jobs move.

77
00:02:46,332 --> 00:02:48,842
A prettier input queue is not the finish line.

78
00:02:48,842 --> 00:02:50,458
The green completed jobs are.

79
00:02:50,467 --> 00:02:51,636
Keep eight workers.

80
00:02:51,636 --> 00:02:53,004
Open two more slots.

81
00:02:53,004 --> 00:02:54,604
Four jobs pass together.

82
00:02:54,604 --> 00:02:56,226
Watch the green side fill.

83
00:02:56,226 --> 00:02:57,678
Last four coming through.

84
00:02:57,700 --> 00:02:59,751
Six point five simulated seconds.

85
00:02:59,751 --> 00:03:01,304
This time the finish moved.

86
00:03:01,304 --> 00:03:05,757
The orange pile clears in bigger waves because the doorway actually got wider.

87
00:03:05,767 --> 00:03:09,917
Watch again: same jobs, same service time, four slots.

88
00:03:09,917 --> 00:03:14,879
That capacity switch belongs to this simulator, not your provider's control panel.

89
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:17,687
No magic setting appeared in a real API.

90
00:03:17,687 --> 00:03:19,557
We widened this simulated door.

91
00:03:19,557 --> 00:03:21,185
Your turn to change an input.

92
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:21,831
Rematch.

93
00:03:21,831 --> 00:03:24,865
I'm stretching preparation from half a second to three.

94
00:03:24,865 --> 00:03:26,813
Watch the blue blocks hang around.

95
00:03:26,813 --> 00:03:29,363
Now the doorway can run out of ready jobs again.

96
00:03:29,367 --> 00:03:30,311
There is the gap.

97
00:03:30,311 --> 00:03:32,583
A different input, a different race.

98
00:03:32,583 --> 00:03:37,194
Run this exact simulator and change that value before you add another worker.

99
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:38,890
Keep the job numbers visible.

100
00:03:38,890 --> 00:03:41,687
Count what finishes, not how busy the screen looks.

101
00:03:41,687 --> 00:03:45,155
And yes, worker four's little comment was intentional.

102
00:03:45,167 --> 00:03:47,393
Make your next guess with the doorway in view.

103
00:03:47,393 --> 00:03:48,400
Then press run.

104
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:50,923
The orange pile will tell you where to look.
